- Setup failures are inputs with no planted triple (2 of 4 cells at s \= 2 and 3, 1 of 4 at s \= 4), as in m83; they are not attempts, and their setup cost is not in the per-attempt averages.
- Timeouts are charged their full deadline (about 5 s of solver time) to the engine. F4-style and F5B time out at s \>\= 3 and Z3 reaches its deadline at s \= 4 on some cells, so their totals at larger s are set by the deadline, not by an algorithm\'s completion time.
- #strong[Deviation from m83]: this host\'s solver stage is faster than m83\'s (section 8), and several cells near the 5 s deadline completed here that m83 recorded as timeouts: Z3 at s \= 4 and one F5B cell at s \= 3 (9 cells over 3 repetitions, listed in `results/verify_report.json`). Cells whose status changed between repetitions are named in the table. A timeout at a fixed 5 s deadline is a property of the host speed as much as of the engine.
- At s \= 4 the solver stage is no longer small next to equation build, and CryptoMiniSat\'s total is below FES\'s (436.0 ms against 507.8 ms per attempt), as in m83\'s solver-stage ranking. No natural relation was found at any size.

